---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const title = 'Wanderburg Best Modules — Slot Reference (0.9.9 EA)';
const description =
  'Wanderburg module answers: starter four slots, Front Cannon unlock at side-cannon 10, Companion back slot, and what to mount first for turrets, fire+ballista, and mortar.';
const modulesStill =
  'https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3624140/36b03816140674eb040db96cec090854044dff5d/ss_36b03816140674eb040db96cec090854044dff5d.1920x1080.jpg';
const ogImage = modulesStill;
const heroSrc = '/images/ss_36b03816140674eb040db96cec090854044dff5d.1920x1080.jpg';

const showcase = [
  { name: 'Side Cannons', slot: 'Side', blurb: 'Auto-fire + broadside ability. Core day-one gun.', stat: 'Unlock → Front Cannon at Lv10' },
  { name: 'Front Ram', slot: 'Front', blurb: 'Hit + shove ahead. Helps Overtime mobility.', stat: 'Unlock → Arms at Lv10' },
  { name: 'Top Mortar', slot: 'Top', blurb: 'Area volley / bombard from the roof.', stat: 'Some hulls get two top slots' },
  { name: 'Mine Layer', slot: 'Back', blurb: 'Drop mines while you kite. Spiderberg has no back.', stat: 'Pairs with Companion routes' },
];
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} ogImage={ogImage} canonicalPath="/best-modules/" shell="parchment">
  <div class="guide-layout">
    <div class="parchment-panel">
      <img
        class="hero-img"
        src={heroSrc}
        alt="Wanderburg Choose New Module UI"
        width="1920"
        height="1080"
        fetchpriority="high"
      />
      <p class="hero-caption">Pick a slot. Mount a gun. Buy it later with silver.</p>

      <h1>Wanderburg Best Modules — Slot Guide</h1>
      <p class="lead" style="text-align:center;">
        Starter slots, Front Cannon unlock, Companion back slot, and what to mount first by family.
      </p>
      <span class="hero-divider" aria-hidden="true" style="margin:0.5rem auto 1rem;display:block;"></span>

      <div class="module-showcase" role="list">
        {showcase.map((m) => (
          <article class="module-card" role="listitem">
            <span class="mod-slot">{m.slot}</span>
            <h3>{m.name}</h3>
            <p>{m.blurb}</p>
            <div class="mod-stat">{m.stat}</div>
            <a class="cta-btn" href="#starter-slots">View details →</a>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>

      <h2 id="starter-slots">How do I set the four starter slots?</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Answer:</strong> Day one, park <strong>side cannons on side</strong>, <strong>ram on front</strong>, <strong>mortar on top</strong>, and <strong>mine layer on back</strong> — that’s the default kit every EA tape starts from.
      </p>
      <p>
        Side cannons auto-fire and also have a broadside ability on Q/E/R/Space. Ram shoves what’s ahead (handy when Overtime gets spicy). Mortar dumps an area volley from the roof. Mines drop behind you while you kite.
      </p>
      <p>
        Hull caveat: some vehicles get <strong>two top</strong> slots; <strong>Spiderberg has no back</strong>. Bindings are Q / E / R / Space plus auto-attacks. Relics that buff “all top,” “all back,” or “all arrow abilities” are the ones worth grabbing once you’ve picked a family.
      </p>
      <div class="slot-diagram" aria-label="Module slot layout">
        <div class="slot slot-wide"><strong>Top</strong> mortar · fire mage · (some hulls: two top)</div>
        <div class="slot"><strong>Side</strong> cannons · ballista · barracks</div>
        <div class="slot"><strong>Front</strong> ram · front cannon</div>
        <div class="slot"><strong>Back</strong> mines · Companion · booster</div>
      </div>
      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr><th>Slot</th><th>Starter</th><th>Job</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td><strong>Side</strong></td><td>Side cannons</td><td>Side shots + broadside</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Front</strong></td><td>Front ram</td><td>Hit + shove ahead</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Top</strong></td><td>Top mortar</td><td>Area volley / bombard</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Back</strong></td><td>Mine layer</td><td>Drop mines while you kite</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h2 id="front-cannon">Side cannons — what level unlocks Front Cannon?</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Answer:</strong> Push <strong>side cannons to upgrade level 10</strong>, then the game toasts Front Cannon — you still <strong>buy it in the loadout</strong> with silver.
      </p>
      <p>
        Same pattern for the ram line: ram to level 10 unlocks <strong>Arms</strong>, then purchase. Unlock toast ≠ owned. Silver pays between runs — see <a href="/silver-farming/">Silver farming</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        Other loadout buys once unlocked: Turret Layer, Side Ballista, Fire Crew, Side Barracks, Companion, Fire Mage. Archer crew to level 10 unlocks Archer Tower on fewer tapes. No shop price grid here.
      </p>
      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr><th>Do this</th><th>Opens (then buy)</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>Side cannons → level 10</td><td>Front Cannon</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Ram → level 10</td><td>Arms</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Archer crew → level 10</td><td>Archer Tower</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Destroy 100 health boxes overall</td><td>Repair Crew</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Beat all four Golden Dunes bosses</td><td>Spiderberg (still buy)</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h2 id="companion-slot">Companion — which slot do I have to keep?</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Answer:</strong> Companion is a <strong>back</strong> module — keep a back slot free, which means <strong>skip Spiderberg</strong> for that run.
      </p>
      <p>
        Companion spawns a hammer robot. With Empress you get two Companions; she also halves your speed, so bring ram / booster / nitro if you plan Overtime. Side Barracks sits in the same friendly-unit neighborhood.
      </p>
      <p>
        Want mines instead? Fine — just don’t expect Companion on a no-back hull. Full captain pairing: <a href="/captains/">Captains</a>.
      </p>

      <h2 id="families">Turrets+arrows / fire+ballista / mortar — what do I mount first?</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Answer:</strong> Pick <strong>one</strong> family and feed it — turrets want Turret Layer + arrow kit, fire wants Fire Crew + Side Ballista, mortar wants Top mortar next to your side cannons.
      </p>

      <h3>Turrets + arrows</h3>
      <p>
        Mount <strong>Turret Layer</strong> first, then chase Archer Tower, Side Ballista, and archer crew. Drop the turret, kite, scoop gold for level-ups.
      </p>
      <p>
        Grab the relic that shortens all arrow ability CDs when you kill with arrows — that’s the engine. One tape claimed a #1 leaderboard run with this pile; treat it as “players like it,” not a promise.
      </p>

      <h3>Fire + ballista</h3>
      <p>
        Mount <strong>Fire Crew + Side Ballista</strong> together. Vehicles that die from fire leave fire craters — that’s the synergy creators chase on Golden Dunes clips.
      </p>
      <p>
        Fire Mage exists in EA, but Demo 8 “mage tower is broken” titles are a different balance conversation. Don’t import demo power claims.
      </p>

      <h3>Cannons + mortar</h3>
      <p>
        Keep <strong>side cannons</strong>, push them toward Front Cannon, and park <strong>Top mortar</strong> on the roof. Pair with <a href="/captains/">Patchy the Pirate</a> if you want the cannon-damage captain line.
      </p>
      <p>
        Magma Core (cannonballs leave a fire grid) shows up on the same cannon tapes. If a roll says “cannonball” next to mortar, read the tooltip — don’t assume every cannon relic applies.
      </p>

      <h3>Also solid (not a fourth family you must chase)</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Ram + mines</strong> — mobility for Overtime; bumper ram + mine dumps show up on silver grind streams.</li>
        <li><strong>Merchants crew</strong> — passive gold → faster levels. Not a gun. Skip late merchant rolls if you never invested early.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>When to take / skip a roll</h2>
      <div class="decision-tree">
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Position relic matches your slots</strong> (all top / all back / all arrow) → take it.</li>
          <li><strong>Off-theme shiny</strong> while your core isn’t online → skip. Finish the family first.</li>
          <li><strong>Only back slot left on an Empress run</strong> → Companion (or Booster if Companion is already set).</li>
          <li><strong>Demo mage-tower nostalgia</strong> → skip.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="crosslinks">
        <strong>Next:</strong>
        <a href="/silver-farming/">Silver farming</a> ·
        <a href="/captains/">Captains</a> ·
        <a href="/">Home</a>
      </div>

      <details class="still-checking">
        <summary>Still checking</summary>
        <ul>
          <li>Shop silver prices — no verified grid.</li>
          <li>Exact slots for Cannon Tower / Arms / Force Mage — best-effort only.</li>
          <li>0.9.9 patch string not confirmed on Steam news.</li>
        </ul>
      </details>
    </div>

    <aside class="guide-side" aria-label="Quick reference">
      <div class="side-panel">
        <h2>Slot Reference</h2>
        <div class="slot-ref-row">
          <span>Front</span>
          <span>Sides</span>
          <span>Back</span>
        </div>
        <p style="font-size:0.78rem;margin:0.65rem 0 0;opacity:0.9;">
          Top sits above the hull. Some hulls get two top slots. Spiderberg has no back.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="side-panel tips-board">
        <h2>Do This Now</h2>
        <ol>
          <li>Starter four: <strong>cannons / ram / mortar / mines</strong>.</li>
          <li>Side cannons to <strong>level 10</strong> → Front Cannon unlock.</li>
          <li>Companion needs <strong>back</strong> — skip Spiderberg.</li>
          <li>Pick one family: turrets, fire+ballista, or cannons+mortar.</li>
          <li>Unlock toast ≠ owned — <a href="/silver-farming/">farm silver</a>.</li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </aside>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
